From aa4e9e6ebe4a04e1bd63ad01c13852ab728a00f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steven Lee <steven_lee@aspeedtech.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:32:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mctp: add AST2700 I3C target network transport

Add an AF_MCTP point-to-point network interface for local I3C targets
selected by the mctp-controller property. Implement software PEC and
worker-based pending-read notification with a baseline transmit MTU.

Add synchronized target receive callbacks, initialize target hardware
before probing its client, and handle AST2700 transfer errors and cleanup.
Keep character-device and network target bindings mutually exclusive.
Enable the transport for AST2700 DC-SCM and document setup and limitations.
Disable the legacy controller and target MCTP character-device drivers in
aspeed_g7_defconfig, retaining both AF_MCTP I3C transports.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Steven Lee <steven_lee@aspeedtech.com>
---
